Embedded React: measure auto-height flexWrap rows at their available width.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json. Changed files: engine/layout/
layout_engine.c and engine/tests/layout/test_yoga_parity.c. Upstream:
https://github.com/TheMasterCoder007/embedded-react/pull/281 — drop this patch
once the pinned revision includes the fix.

measure_content() summed every child onto one line, so an auto-height
`flexWrap: 'wrap'` row reserved a single line's height and its wrapped lines
overflowed onto the following siblings. The measurement now receives the width
the parent offers and breaks the row into lines as Yoga does.

